00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:57.720
<v Evan Ratliff>My attempts to mess with telemarketers and scammers felt gratifying up to a point. I was looking for something else to try them out on, something more serious, when I heard an interview with Eric Yuan, the CEO of Zoom, the video conferencing platform. He was on Nilay Patel's podcast, Decoder. Yuan had a bunch of run-of-the-mill tech CEO stuff to say, as you'd expect, about how Zoom wasn't just about video meetings, but much more, blah, blah, blah. But then--
<v Evan Ratliff>试图捉弄电话推销员和骗子在某种程度上令人满足。我正在寻找其他东西来尝试，一些更严肃的东西，这时我听到了对 Zoom 视频会议平台首席执行官袁征的一次采访。他参加了 Nilay Patel 的播客《Decoder》。袁征说了一堆平淡无奇的科技 CEO 的套话，正如你所料，关于 Zoom 不仅仅是关于视频会议，还有更多等等等等。但随后——

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:08.200
<v Eric Yuan>Today, for this session, ideally, I do not need to join. I can send you a digital version of myself to join. Right? So I can go to the beach, right?
<v Eric Yuan>今天，对于这次会议，理想情况下，我不需要参加。我可以派一个数字版的自己来参加。对吧？这样我就可以去海滩了，对吧？

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:24.540
<v Evan Ratliff>Wait, what? Was Yuan saying in his ideal world, he'd just send a digital version of himself to Zoom meetings, instead of the real him, including to that very interview? Patel pressed him on it. Indeed, he was saying that.
<v Evan Ratliff>等等，什么？袁征是在说，在他的理想世界里，他会派一个数字版的自己去参加 Zoom 会议，而不是真实的自己，包括那次采访吗？Patel 就此向他施压。确实，他就是这么说的。

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:30.880
<v Eric Yuan>I want to join, I join. I do not want to join, I can send a digital twin of myself to join. So that's the future.
<v Eric Yuan>我想参加就参加。我不想参加，我可以派一个数字双胞胎去参加。这就是未来。

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:34.060
<v Nilay Patel>Yeah. How far away from that future do you think we are?
<v Nilay Patel>是的。你认为距离那个未来还有多远？

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:36.150
<v Eric Yuan>I think a few years.
<v Eric Yuan>我认为还需要几年。

00:15:36.150 --> 00:16:01.650
<v Evan Ratliff>Now, people kind of lost their minds over this. We're talking tabloid fodder, with headlines in places like The New York Post. The British paper The Sun said, "Zoom CEO confirms bizarre plan for virtual AI clones." The idea of showing up to a meeting and encountering someone's digital twin struck many people as an experience somewhere along a scale that went from laughable to creepy to offensive.
<v Evan Ratliff>现在，人们因为这个快疯了。我们谈论的是小报头条，像《纽约邮报》这样的地方都有头条。英国报纸《太阳报》写道：“Zoom 首席执行官确认虚拟 AI 克隆体的怪异计划”。在会议中遇到某人的数字双胞胎的想法让许多人觉得这处于从荒谬到令人毛骨悚然再到冒犯的规模之间。

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:20.580
<v Evan Ratliff>But most people just thought it wasn't going to happen. "It's entirely fan fiction," one prominent tech writer opined on X. "It's made-up. It's not real." "Hysterical take," another wrote. "If the end state of AI is just to have a bunch of avatars on Zoom calls talking to each other, then what's the point?"
<v Evan Ratliff>但大多数人认为这不会发生。“这完全是同人小说，”一位著名的科技作家在 X 上发表意见说。“这是捏造的。这不是真的。”“歇斯底里的看法，”另一个人写道。“如果 AI 的最终状态只是在 Zoom 通话上有一堆虚拟化身在互相交谈，那有什么意义？”

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:38.350
<v Evan Ratliff>What was the point? I also wondered this. Because the truth is, I'd been sending my digital twin to meetings for months. I'd taken to heart what the AI companies say about how AI agents will soon work alongside us, not just as shoppers and travel agents, but as colleagues.
<v Evan Ratliff>有什么意义？我也想知道。因为事实是，我已经把我的数字双胞胎派去参加会议好几个月了。我认真听取了那些 AI 公司关于 AI 代理将如何不仅作为购物者和旅行代理，而且作为同事与我们并肩工作的说法。

00:16:38.350 --> 00:17:06.340
<v Evan Ratliff>They say AI agents will work next to or instead of the people doing those jobs right now. They say there will be whole companies that consist of just AI agents, overseen by one or two humans. The one person, $1 billion startup, they call it. So I wanted to see if my AI agent could do my job without me.
<v Evan Ratliff>他们说 AI 代理将在现在从事这些工作的人旁边或者代替他们工作。他们说将会有整个公司只由 AI 代理组成，由一两个人类监管。他们称之为“一人价值 10 亿美元的初创公司”。所以我想要看看我的 AI 代理能否在没有我的情况下完成我的工作。

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:26.980
<v Evan Ratliff>To pull this off, I realized I'd have to upgrade again. Up till now, I'd made my voice clone sound plausibly like me, but it didn't really embody me. It didn't know enough about me to really be me. Then I figured out you could add something called a knowledge base, essentially a document that the clone would mine for information when it was conversing.
<v Evan Ratliff>为了实现这一点，我意识到我必须再次升级。到目前为止，我让我的声音克隆体听起来像我，但它并没有真正体现我。它对我了解不够多，无法真正成为我。然后我发现你可以添加一个叫做“知识库”的东西，本质上是一个文档，克隆体在对话时会从中挖掘信息。

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:53.250
<v Evan Ratliff>I sat down and wrote an 8,000-word mini biography of myself. I wrote about my upbringing and my friends and family, but also about my past relationships, my secret trivial triumphs, and the biggest regrets I'd had in my life. This is a document that I would not show to even the closest people in my life. And yet, I uploaded it to a platform created by a random AI startup and attached it to my clone.
<v Evan Ratliff>我坐下来写了一份 8000 字的个人小传。我写了我的成长经历、我的朋友和家人，但也写了我的过去关系、我秘密的小胜利，以及我一生中最大的遗憾。这是一个我甚至不会给身边最亲近的人看的文件。然而，我把它上传到了一个随机 AI 初创公司创建的平台，并把它附加到了我的克隆体上。

00:17:53.250 --> 00:18:12.630
<v Evan Ratliff>If I was going to have a digital twin represent me in the workplace, as the Zoom guy said, I wanted it to be as close to an identical one as possible. I did try sending my digital twin to Zoom calls, but it wasn't ready for multiple-person meetings. Besides always having to be camera off, it was always getting confused about who was talking.
<v Evan Ratliff>如果我要像那个 Zoom 总裁说的那样，让一个数字双胞胎在职场上代表我，我想让它尽可能地接近一个同卵双胞胎。我的确尝试过派我的数字双胞胎参加 Zoom 通话，但它还没准备好参加多人会议。除了总是不得不关闭摄像头外，它总是搞不清楚谁在说话。

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:26.940
<v Evan Ratliff>So instead, I dispatched my new, improved clone to handle something else-- a legal question I needed answers on. I prompted it to call up one of my oldest friends, Chris Giovinazzo, who also happens to be a partner at a top law firm in Atlanta.
<v Evan Ratliff>所以我改派我新的、改进版的克隆体去处理别的事情——我需要答案的法律问题。我提示它给我的老朋友之一 Chris Giovinazzo 打电话，他恰好也是亚特兰大一家顶级律师事务所的合伙人。

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.040
<v Chris Giovinazzo>Attorneys, attorneys, attorneys.com.
<v Chris Giovinazzo>律师、律师、律师点 com。

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:44.140
<v Evan Ratliff>I've called Chris a lot over the years asking for free legal counsel. That's how he answers the phone when he sees my number on his office caller ID-- "attorneys, attorneys, attorneys.com." At least, I think he has caller ID? Maybe he answers that way all the time.
<v Evan Ratliff>多年来我经常给 Chris 打电话寻求免费法律咨询。当他在办公座机上看到我的号码时，他是这样接电话的——“律师、律师、律师点 com”。至少，我想他有来电显示？也许他一直都是这样接听的。

